version: "0.5.0"

date-released: 2026-08-16

abstract: >
  CPC Validation is the reference validation framework for
  C-Parity Computing (CPC). It defines a canonical constraint IR,
  qualified RC, Digital, and FPGA execution backends, independent
  cross-backend semantic validation, and an RFC-0009 physical-evidence
  lifecycle. This release includes the first recorded P1 execution on
  a Lattice iCE40 UltraPlus Breakout Board, with deterministic build and
  timing artifacts, guarded device-programming evidence, restricted LED
  observation, concrete evidence-profile conformance, and independent
  post-execution CCIR validation.

